[stage0] NON-BLOCKING: initial tests/test_environment.py::test_gemmi_roundtrip failed twice using a hand-built minimal synthetic mmCIF block (gemmi.make_structure_from_block / gemmi.read_structure both returned 0 models). Root cause not fully diagnosed (likely a missing required mmCIF field for gemmi's structure-builder heuristics). Resolved by rewriting the test to read an actual extracted SD-H .cif file instead of a synthetic minimal block, which is also more representative of real pipeline usage. Final test suite: 6 passed, 0 failed. Does not block Stage 0 completion.
[stage0] NON-BLOCKING DATA ISSUE (resolved): APFS case-insensitive filesystem caused 18 archive members across 5 archives to collide with an existing same-named-except-case file during extraction (e.g. chain "B" vs "b"). safe_extract.py originally logged these as CONFLICT_NOT_OVERWRITTEN (data would have been missing, not lost, but incomplete). Fixed by adding case-collision detection to safe_extract.py: colliding members are now extracted under a disambiguated `__casecollision2` filename with the mapping recorded in data/metadata/extraction_manifest.tsv. All extractions were re-run after the fix; 0 unresolved conflicts remain.
